<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SOS-09 umbrella §12 gate (c) worked-example fixture: ONE chart channel
  threaded end-to-end through all six SOS-09 emit paths. Closes the
  load-bearing demonstration of "single source of truth across the
  hardware/software membrane".

  Channel under test:

    sos:id              11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
    sos:name            telemetry_status
    sos:kind            status            (§5.1 — recommended by gate (c))
    sos:dir             hw→sw             (§5.2 arrow form; ERRATA-004 alignment)
    sos:zone            privileged        (§5.4 v1 enumeration; PCDN-SOS-09-006)
    sos:atomicity       atomic            (§5.3 default for status; declared explicitly)
    sos:width           32                (single-register, atomic single-cycle)
    sos:irq             telemetry_ready   (PCDN-SOS-SOS-09-004 logical IRQ name)
    sos:channel_group   telemetry         (PCDN-SOS-09-007 Rust borrow scope)
    sos:privilege_region telemetry        (PCDN-SOS-09-007 HDL MPU scope;
                                           inherits from channel_group)
    sos:bit_layout      {ready: bit 0 RO clear-on-read; count: bits 1..7 RO;
                         reserved_hi: bits 8..31 reserved}

  Six emit paths the single channel drives (gate (c) acceptance surface):

    1. SOS-09-B CMSIS-SVD   → tools/sos-codegen/transliterate_svd.py
                              emits <peripheral><registers><register name="telemetry_status">
                              plus <interrupt name="telemetry_ready">
    2. SOS-09-B SystemRDL   → DEFERRED per SOS-09-B §16 + PCDN-SOS-09-B-005(a):
                              "future sibling sub-phase (e.g. SOS-09-B2-SYSTEMRDL)
                              when a non-Cortex-M target enters the SOS bench
                              substrate". Test cleanly skips with the deferral
                              citation as reason.
    3. SOS-09-C C HAL       → tools/sos-codegen/c_hal_emit.py
                              emits sos_<chart>__telemetry.h with
                              SOS_C_telemetry_status_* accessors (clear-on-read
                              field drives _consume_* naming per gate (f)).
    4. SOS-09-D Rust HAL    → tools/sos-codegen/transliterate_rust.py
                              emits src/lib.rs with a ClearOnRead<u32> newtype
                              for the channel (gate (d) family completeness)
                              and the SOS_MPU_TELEMETRY_STATUS_REGION const.
    5. SOS-09-E HDL regfile → tools/sos-codegen/transliterate_regfile.py
                              emits sos_regfile_<peripheral>.{vhd,sv} with
                              the channel as an output register + strobe-latch
                              aggregated into the "telemetry" privilege region.
    6. SOS-09-F membrane    → tools/sos-codegen/vectors_emit.py
       vectors                emits per-family test_*.py files; the channel's
                              UUID appears in the MV-<UUID>-<family>-<seq>
                              trace-key chain.

  Cross-validation property (the gate-(c) deliverable):

    The single sos:id UUID `11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111` and the
    single sos:name `telemetry_status` MUST appear as a recognizable trace
    in every emitted artifact. The companion test
    `test_sos_09_six_emitter_end_to_end.py` asserts this end-to-end.

  Per SOS-09 umbrella §16 (2026-05-27 acceptance roll-up): "no single chart
  channel currently threads end-to-end through all six emit paths" was
  the explicit ⏸ reason for gate (c). This fixture is the unification
  that flips the gate ✅. (ERRATA-004 cite: sos:dir uses the arrow form
  `hw→sw` per the SOS-09-A §5.2 alignment.)

  Per SOS-09-A §5.1, allowed parent contexts for channel annotations are
  <state> and <parallel>; this chart uses <state> for the single channel
  (the umbrella demonstration does not require a parallel region — one
  channel is the gate-(c) minimum).

  Per PCDN-SOS-09-001 amended 2026-05-25: sos: keys are JSON-key strings
  inside other_attributes JSON, not XML namespace declarations. NO
  xmlns:sos declaration appears in this chart.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       version="1.0"
       datamodel="ecmascript"
       initial="TELEMETRY_STATUS_CH"
       other_attributes='{"sos:mpu_background": "kernel_default"}'>

  <state id="TELEMETRY_STATUS_CH"
         other_attributes='{
           "sos:id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
           "sos:name": "telemetry_status",
           "sos:kind": "status",
           "sos:dir": "hw→sw",
           "sos:zone": "privileged",
           "sos:atomicity": "atomic",
           "sos:width": 32,
           "sos:irq": "telemetry_ready",
           "sos:channel_group": "telemetry",
           "sos:privilege_region": "telemetry",
           "sos:bit_layout": {
             "fields": [
               {"name": "ready", "start_bit": 0, "width": 1, "access": "RO", "side_effect": "clear-on-read", "reset_value": 0},
               {"name": "count", "start_bit": 1, "width": 7, "access": "RO", "side_effect": null, "reset_value": 0},
               {"name": "reserved_hi", "start_bit": 8, "width": 24, "access": "reserved", "side_effect": null, "reset_value": 0}
             ]
           }
         }'>
    <transition event="reset" target="TELEMETRY_STATUS_CH"/>
  </state>

</scxml>
